course: dictionary
lesson: 3470
title: Faithfully: one word, four meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around the word tells you which one to use. Look at the clues first. «The dog waited faithfully by the gate every day.» A dog that waits every day for its owner is loyal, so faithfully means in a loyal way that can be trusted.
explain: The same word can mean something different in a different sentence. «Please copy the list faithfully.» Here there is no loyal dog. The clue is copy: faithfully means exactly, with no changes. Always ask what fits, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: In letters, «Yours faithfully» is a set ending. You use it when you begin with «Dear Sir or Madam», because you do not know the person's name. Read the start of the letter, and the ending will make sense.
fact: Faithfully means in a loyal way that can be trusted, keeping promises and staying true.
fact: Faithfully means exactly and carefully, without changes, as in «copied faithfully».
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, «Yours faithfully» ends a formal letter that begins «Dear Sir or Madam».
fact: Faithfully can also mean with religious faith and devotion, as in church.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The dog waited faithfully by the gate for its owner every day.» What does faithfully mean here? | *In a loyal way that can be trusted | Very fast and noisily | Sadly, with tears | Once, long ago
exercise: «The clerk copied the list faithfully, without changing a single word.» What does faithfully mean here? | Quickly and messily | Angrily, with a loud voice | *Exactly and carefully, with no changes
exercise: Which ending do you use for a formal letter that begins «Dear Sir or Madam»? | Love from | See you later | Hip hip hooray | *Yours faithfully
test: «I faithfully promise I will come back.» What does faithfully mean here? | Quietly, so no one hears | *Truly and seriously, keeping my word | Slowly, one step at a time | Happily, with a song
test: «She prayed faithfully every morning in church.» What does faithfully mean here? | With loud music playing | *With religious faith and devotion | Carelessly, forgetting the words | Only sometimes, when she felt like it
exam: «Keep small promises faithfully even when nobody would find out.» Which word means the same as faithfully here? | Rarely | Loudly | Quickly | *Honestly and loyally
